<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! face.roster.reads ~ read the vessel's own roster

The read answers the vessel's own reading of its seats, lanes and vota, and moves nothing.

The address stands ''candidate'' until the operator reads the landing's list. The MCP seat runs this act in its own process: the vessel's `call` binds the params against this carrier's live `#/takes` and answers `handler/seat` with the bound params, and the seat runs them (`act(address="lar:///face.roster.reads", args={…})`).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ nothing

```memetic-wikitext

```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ seat

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`seat` params=`who/seat-or-hand ~ the vessel verbs the seat's handler reaches check the face's cap and the asker's hand themselves; a hand act refuses a seat by its own code`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

